A spinning indicator that shows a loading state.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/spinner)

<%= embed UI::SpinnerPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Spinner()
Button(disabled: true) do
  Spinner(current_color: true, class: "text-[1.2em]")
  plain "Saving…"
end
```

Spinner is a small, self-contained loading indicator - use it whenever something is happening and you can't
show progress. Three shapes via `variant:`: `:circular` (the default sweep), `:dots` (a ring of fading ticks)
and `:sparkle` (a morphing four-point star).

It's sized by font-size, so set a `text-*` class (or inherit `1em` from a parent), and `current_color: true`
takes the surrounding text color instead of the primary accent - what you want inside a colored button. The
animation is SVG SMIL, so it runs without JavaScript; under `prefers-reduced-motion` a static frame is shown.

For a wider "this section is loading" indicator, use [Loader](<%= page_path(:loader) %>).

