### In a button

Show a spinner while the action runs: `current_color:` matches the button text, `text-[1.2em]` scales with
the button, and the button is disabled meanwhile. The second pairs the sparkle variant with an "Ask AI" affordance.

<%= embed UI::SpinnerPreview, :in_button %>

With Turbo you can get this without JavaScript: render the spinner hidden inside the submit button and reveal
it while the form submits (Turbo sets `aria-busy` on the form, so give the form `class: "group"`):

```ruby
Button(type: "submit", class: "group-aria-busy:pointer-events-none") do
  Spinner(current_color: true, class: "hidden text-[1.2em] group-aria-busy:inline-flex")
  plain "Save changes"
end
```

### Refresh button

In an icon button, swap the icon for a spinner - the button keeps its size, so the layout never jumps.

