## API reference

Spinner renders a single `<span role="status">`; other attributes are forwarded to it.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:circular`, `:dots`, `:sparkle` | `:circular` | The animated shape. |
| `current_color:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Inherit the surrounding text color instead of the primary accent. |
| `aria_label:` | `String` | `"Loading"` | Accessible name for the status region. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes, merged via tailwind_merge. Set a `text-*` size here. |

## Accessibility

- The spinner is a `role="status"` live region labelled "Loading"; give it a more specific `aria_label:`
  ("Saving") when the context warrants it.
- Inside a button, the button's own text ("Saving…") is the accessible name - the spinner reinforces it visually.
- A purely decorative spinner beside text that already conveys the state can be `aria_hidden: true`.
- The animation is replaced by a static frame when the user prefers reduced motion.
